USP Connections is a network of local academic reception programs coordinated by USP academic units or students. In each unit, USP students (undergraduate or graduate) can take part in welcoming and supporting international students during their stay at USP.
What kind of support can be offered?
Arrival support – guiding or picking up the student at the airport and helping them reach their first destination (home, hostel, or campus);
Housing – assisting the student in finding accommodation, offering advice about neighborhoods, transportation, and rental options;
Legal procedures – helping the student understand the steps related to visa registration and regularization at the Federal Police;
Academic life – sharing tips on how to enroll in courses, use libraries, access online systems, and get involved with student groups;
Language practice – supporting students in improving their Portuguese through conversation and everyday interactions;
Cultural integration – introducing the student to the local culture by showing them how to use public transportation, visit museums, attend events, and more.
